<article class="glass-card rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-8 text-slate-300">
  <div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-3">
      How to Calculate Late Payment Interest & Invoicing Penalties
    </h2>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Late client payments disrupt cash flow and create severe financial stress for freelancers and small agency owners. Charging a fair statutory interest rate or flat late payment fee compensates you for delayed capital and encourages corporate clients to process payments on time.
    </p>
  </div>

  {/* Formula Box */}
  <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 space-y-3">
    <h3 class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-rose-400">
      Late Fee Interest Calculation Formula
    </h3>
    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-rose-950/40 border border-rose-500/30 text-center font-mono text-sm sm:text-base text-white font-bold">
      Late Interest = Invoice Amount × (Annual Interest Rate / 365) × Days Overdue
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      Daily simple interest is calculated by dividing the agreed annual late fee percentage by 365 days and multiplying by the total number of days past the invoice due date.
    </p>
  </div>

  {/* Worked Numerical Example */}
  <div class="space-y-4">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
      Worked Numerical Example: Overdue $4,000 Invoice
    </h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Consider an invoice of $4,000 that is 45 days overdue, with a standard contract clause specifying a 18% annual late interest rate (1.5% monthly):
    </p>

    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 space-y-2 text-xs font-mono">
      <div class="flex justify-between text-slate-400"><span>1. Principal Invoice Amount:</span><span class="text-slate-200">$4,000.00</span></div>
      <div class="flex justify-between text-slate-400"><span>2. Daily Interest Rate (18% / 365):</span><span class="text-slate-200">0.049315% per day</span></div>
      <div class="flex justify-between text-slate-400"><span>3. Overdue Duration:</span><span class="text-slate-200">45 days</span></div>
      <div class="flex justify-between text-white font-bold border-t border-slate-800 pt-1.5"><span>Accrued Late Fee Interest:</span><span class="text-rose-400">$88.77</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-rose-950/30 border border-rose-500/30 text-xs text-slate-200 font-mono font-bold flex justify-between">
      <span>Updated Balance Due:</span>
      <span class="text-rose-400 text-sm">$4,088.77</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* Practical Freelancer Advice */}
  <div class="space-y-3">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
      Legally Enforcing Late Fees Without Damaging Client Relationships
    </h3>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      <li><strong>State Terms on the Original Contract & Invoice:</strong> Late fees cannot be enforced retroactively. You must state late fee terms (e.g., "1.5% monthly interest on balances past 30 days") in your contract before work begins.</li>
      <li><strong>Send Automated Reminder Notices:</strong> Send courtesy reminders 7 days before due date, on due date, and at 7 days past due before applying interest charges.</li>
      <li><strong>Know Statutory Late Payment Rates:</strong> In the UK, the Late Payment of Commercial Debts Act allows charging 8% plus the Bank of England base rate on commercial debts.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  {/* Frequently Asked Questions */}
  <div class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-800">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">
      Frequently Asked Questions About Invoice Late Fees
    </h3>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-sm">
      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">What is a reasonable late fee percentage for business invoices?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">The most common commercial late fee rate is 1.5% per month (which equals 18% per year), or a flat fee of $25 to $50 for smaller balances.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">Can I legally charge late fees if it was not in the original contract?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">In many jurisdictions, commercial law allows statutory interest even without explicit contract terms (such as the UK Commercial Debts Act). However, in the US, late fees generally require prior written notice on the original invoice or agreement.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">Should I waive a late fee if the client promises to pay immediately?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Waiving a first-time late fee as a courtesy can preserve long-term client goodwill, provided you explicitly remind the client that future late payments will incur full penalties.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">How are overdue days calculated?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Overdue days are counted starting from the day immediately following your invoice due date up to the date payment is received in full.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pb-1">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white mb-1">Is this calculation private?</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Yes. SimpleInvoiceTools processes all late fee interest computations 100% locally in your browser.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
